{
  "paper": "Aprea & Sbaiz (2025), Decisions in Economics and Finance, https://doi.org/10.1007/s10203-025-00508-x",
  "comparison_level": "METHOD SUBSTITUTION on the Aprea & Sbaiz DJIA universe (n=28), exact period/schedule. Aprea minimize an aggregate Delta-CoVaR (LSTM-estimated) under ESG/turnover/min-profit constraints; this benchmark keeps the exact-K cardinality mean-variance objective solved by PSO/SA and swaps in MASTER/TFT/PatchTST mu. Not a replication: different objective and constraints, reconstructed public prices. Compared on the shared ex-post metrics (period Sharpe, CAGR).",
  "notes": [
    "Fallback when the Cesarone/Refinitiv sustainability ZIP is unavailable.",
    "Uses the 28-stock DJIA full-history pool aligned with the paper's 31-Dec-2020 investable universe.",
    "Dates and monthly OOS schedule follow Aprea & Sbaiz: daily panel 2006-10-06..2020-12-31, fit through 2015-12-31, monthly OOS 2016-2020.",
    "The paper optimizes Delta-CoVaR with PSO. This thesis benchmark retains the exact-K cardinality-constrained mean-variance objective and compares MASTER/TFT/PatchTST through PSO and SA.",
    "Uses Yahoo Finance auto-adjusted prices for 27 names.",
    "Yahoo no longer reliably serves WBA after its 2025 delisting; WBA adjusted-close history is overlaid from the CC0 Zenodo dataset DOI 10.5281/zenodo.12566460.",
    "WBA is the successor to WAG from 2014-12-31; the public WBA history used here includes the predecessor history and therefore preserves the 2006-2020 panel.",
    "This is still reconstructed public data rather than the paper's Refinitiv/Cesarone file, so it must not be labelled an exact-data replication.",
    "mu-normalization policy: all models calibrated to historical-return scale (calibrate=true); MASTER is rank-only so all three transformers are compared on equal cross-sectional footing.",
    "WINDOWS: moment_frequency is 'daily' (Aprea estimate their moments on MONTHLY returns, but they minimize a CoVaR with no Sigma matrix; our substituted mean-variance objective needs a sample Sigma). On monthly sampling the matched Sigma window (longest conditioning window 336 trading days ~ 16 monthly samples) is rank-deficient for the 28-asset covariance; on daily it is 336 samples (12x oversampled) so Sigma is full-rank while mu stays window-matched (MASTER 67d, TFT 271d, PatchTST 336d). The realized period Sharpe/CAGR follow decision_schedule=month_end + periods_per_year=12 and are unaffected by moment_frequency.",
    "REFIT: Aprea update the in-sample window at EVERY monthly rebalance. Retraining the transformers 59x x 3 seeds is intractable, so model_refit=annual (6 fits) approximates it; moment_refit=match_models keeps Sigma on the same annual cutoffs, and the matched historical mu still rolls every decision (conditioning window, not a refit). Renamed from the obsolete retrain_frequency/covariance_mode/moment_mu_lookback_periods keys.",
    "PORTFOLIO: exact cardinality_K=10 with w_max=0.20 matches Aprea's u_i=0.20 strategy, under which their optimizer holds ~10 assets (Tables 7-8). The u_i=0.06 strategy (~16 assets) is a separate config if needed. w_min=0.01 (Aprea use l_i=0) is required to define an active position under the cardinality constraint."
  ],
